{"type":"assistant_message","payload":{"text":"I read this as completing the `erd-net` transport crate and proving it against the v3 contract - implementation and verification are complete.\n\nImplemented:\n\n- `tls_psk.rs`\n  - OpenSSL vendored TLS client and server with PSK callbacks.\n  - Bootstrap `erd-b1` and paired `erd-p1.<id>` identities.\n  - PBKDF2-SHA256 plus HKDF bootstrap key derivation.\n  - TLS 1.2 PSK AES-GCM cipher suites; TLS 1.3 negotiation disabled for Apple interoperability.\n  - Always-true certificate verification callback.\n  - Incremental 4-byte LE framing with 16 MiB limit and invalid-buffer drop.\n  - Bootstrap failure lockout semantics.\n  - In-process PSK server loopback and partial framing tests.\n\n- `udp_gcm.rs`\n  - AES-256-GCM datagrams with plaintext 12-byte authenticated headers.\n  - Direction-separated HKDF key and nonce chains.\n  - 4-byte prefix plus 8-byte BE counter nonces.\n  - 4096-packet replay window using 64-bit block masks.\n  - RFC 5869 vectors and all six Swift datagram tests, plus exact v3 derivation vectors.\n\n- `signaling.rs`\n  - Deterministic 33-character ntfy topic derivation.\n  - AES-GCM encrypted, Base64 candidate publication.\n  - Required candidate JSON field names and role filtering.\n  - POST status validation and JSONL polling with 10-second deadline.\n  - Live ntfy round-trip test gated by `ERD_LIVE_TESTS=1`.\n\n- `stun.rs`\n  - RFC 5389 binding requests with transaction validation.\n  - XOR-MAPPED-ADDRESS and MAPPED-ADDRESS parsing.\n  - Attribute padding and malformed-response handling.\n  - Default `stun.l.google.com:19302` endpoint.\n\n- Added required dependencies, including direct `openssl-sys` with `vendored`.\n\nVerification:\n\n```text\ncargo test -p erd-net\n24 passed, 0 failed\n\ncargo clippy -p erd-net --all-targets -- -D warnings\nclean\n\ncargo fmt --all -- --check\nclean\n```\n\nLanguage-server diagnostics report no errors."}}
